From 3e44f34f1bb6a25323fa84ee007f5322a73a4d69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 03:54:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: share one hex() test helper in test_util

Every analyzer test module redefined its own `fn hex(&str) -> Vec<u8>`
(four copies, three with an even-length assert and one without), and
test_util had a separate `hex_literal_decode`. Consolidate them into a
single `pub(crate) fn hex` in test_util (asserting an even length so a
mistyped vector fails clearly) and use it everywhere. No behaviour change;
all tests still pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
